      'Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu (BJJ) is the sophisticated martial art and combat science of controlling an resisting opponent on the ground and forcing them to submit through leverage.',
      'Known globally as "the gentle art" (Arte Suave) and "human chess," BJJ was engineered specifically to allow a smaller, physically weaker practitioner to successfully defeat and submit a larger, heavier aggressor.',
      'Unlike striking arts that rely on kinetic impact, BJJ operates on mechanical physics: fulcrums, levers, base of support, wedges, and friction.',
      'A master grappler does not fight force with force; they redirect momentum, pass the opponent’s guard, establish dominant positional control, and apply joint locks or vascular strangles.',
